        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.084,
            0.884,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you think that plants can be grouped on the basis of venation present in their leaves?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.124,
            0.883,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, let us try to "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "explore",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " roots of the plants. Do all plants have roots? Are these roots similar?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.17,
            0.551,
            0.191
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 2.6: Let us find out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.202,
            0.883,
            0.244
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Visit an open area where wild herbs and grasses are growing. You may use small herbs for this exercise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.248,
            0.883,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Using a khurpi (trowel), carefully dig out a few different herbs without damaging the roots. To do this, you may wet the soil and loosen it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.313,
            0.78,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Wash the roots with water and observe them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.339,
            0.883,
            0.38
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " After you are done observing, make sure to replant the herbs so that they may continue to thrive and grow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.384,
            0.885,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What are the similarities and differences in the roots of the plants collected by you? What differences do you see in the roots of plants shown in Fig. 2.5a and Fig. 2.5b?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.317,
            0.453,
            0.545,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": [
